Azure governance can be structured hierarchically so that policies and access configurations applied at higher scopes can influence resources at lower scopes.

The hierarchy commonly follows:

`Management Group → Subscription → Resource Group → Resource`

For example, a policy requiring specific resource tags can be applied at the management group level so that multiple subscriptions inherit the governance requirement.

This approach avoids repeatedly configuring the same policy individually across hundreds of subscriptions.

A real-life use case is an enterprise applying a standard security policy across all production subscriptions from a centralized management group.

Hierarchical governance reduces duplication and helps maintain consistent organizational standards.
